# SHA-256 of the certificate every published Android release is signed with.
# Android replaces an installed app only with a build carrying the same key, and
# the in-app updater depends on exactly that, so the release workflow refuses to
# publish an APK signed with anything else.
#
# Changing this line orphans every phone that installed an earlier release: they
# can only get the new one by uninstalling first. Change it only together with a
# deliberate key rotation, and say so in the release notes.
#
# This is the Android debug key the self-hosted runner generated on 2026-09-10;
# it signs v0.2.2 and v0.2.3. It lives in the runner container's /root/.android,
# which does not survive a rebuild of that container — copy it out and hand it
# to the build through the ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 secret before that happens.
cf317021fde08e1e071d548a146f1f71119b2008f99a7dc918526e009f520c82
